    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "c647f611c3c8316dffd27fc8fa2764de",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1976,
    "chunk_text": "Unfortunately, despite my repeated requests and representations, the Ministry of Defence of the present Government has continuously failed to and refused to provide even the minimum security protocol ordinarily afforded to a Member of Parliament. Such failures have exposed me to a significant personal risk while carrying out my Parliamentary duties and public responsibilities.\n\nI further wish to draw the attention of Parliament to an incident that occurred on my private land, which has been the subject of a long-standing dispute. This matter originated during the tenure of the previous Government and involved former Minister Douglas Devananda, against whom I have raised concerns and regarding attempts to interfere with my ownership and possession of the said land. I have already made a complaint and provided statements before the Magistrate\u2019s Court of Mallakam in relation to this matter in 2023.\n\nSeveral months ago, while acting pursuant to permission granted by the learned Magistrate to enter the land for cleaning and maintenance purposes, I was confronted by individuals affiliated with the former Minister\u2019s political party. During this confrontation, stones were thrown at me, creating an immediate threat to my Secretary's and my personal safety. In response to that threat, I removed the firearm issued for my personal protection from my waist. However, I categorically state that I did not discharge the firearm and not a single shot was fired by me.\n\nFollowing the circulation of media footage relating to the incident, the Ilavalai Police instituted legal proceedings against me despite the fact that I never used the firearm and merely possessed it for personal protection. The matter is presently before courts and the firearm remains in the custody of the Magistrate\u2019s Court of Mallakam.\n\nI reiterate that I have never wished to engage in politics while carrying a firearm. The unfortunate\n\n313 314\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd4"
  },
