    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "35e08c191974aec01e6ae663ec68ff01",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1600,
    "chunk_text": "Having said that, I would now like to refer to a statement made by the Minister in charge of media, who is also the Chief Government Whip. \"No decision to extend the retirement age of Judges: Minister\" reports the \"Daily Mirror\" and goes on to state, \"Amidst controversy over reports of the extension of retirement age of judges, Cabinet Spokesman and Minister Nalinda Jayatissa said yesterday that the Government has not taken any decision, claiming that there has been no discussion on the matter within the Government\". That is not a total denial, but only saying that \"so far, we have not decided.\" But, there is a serious doubt among the public. Also, many organizations, particularly the Bar Association of Sri Lanka and the Colombo High Court Lawyers\u2019 Association have issued statements, warning the Government against that unnecessary attempt to increase the retirement age of judges. We all are bound by what the Bar Association says as we are members of the Bar Association.\n\nMoreover, you are frustrating the judges who have served for years in the Judiciary. What happens to those in the minor Judiciary and others? There is a heavy concern among the Judiciary about extending the retirement age of judges. That creates a different issue; that will block their path and deprive many of their right to be appointed to the Bench or to the Superior Courts. Now, High Court Judges will have to wait for their chances and in expectation of being promoted, undue pressure will be brought upon them. This is a way in which the Constitution is being very deliberately violated by the President."
  },
  {
